  q(HIST,'Which brain surgery, widely used in the 1940s and 1950s, cut connections in the frontal lobes and is now rejected?','Prefrontal lobotomy',['Deep brain stimulation','Transcranial magnetic stimulation','Electroconvulsive therapy'],'B','Lobotomies caused serious harm; antipsychotic drugs replaced them in the 1950s.',PSY)
